# Standalone module changelog rules

- Every registered logical module has one `CHANGELOG.md` at its module root.
- Follow Keep a Changelog and keep `## [Unreleased]` as the first version section.
- Use only populated `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, and `Security` subsections.
- At release, move entries into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`; the version must match `source/libraries/VERSION`.
- Do not add empty release sections to modules that did not change.
- During alpha, summarize the net user-visible delta since the last release, not every code change or MR.
- Changelog edits are not required for routine build fixes, internal cleanup, or test-only changes.
- Revise existing Unreleased entries as features evolve; do not add `Fixed` entries for behavior that has not shipped.
- Omit implementation walkthroughs, commit or issue identifiers, test-only changes, and restated diffs.
- Keep entries concise and identify the affected API when useful.
